  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user with a colour-vision deficiency, I want a topic row to show which flag it carries by something other than the colour of its tint, so that I can tell a favourite from a read flag.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Convey information with more than color alone. Some people have trouble differentiating between certain colors and shades. […] Offer visual indicators, like distinct shapes or icons, in addition to color to help people perceive differences in function and changes in state.\" — [HIG › Accessibility](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility) (Vision; page updated 2025-06-09).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicRowCues.swift:9-16`: the accent is `.yellow` / `.blue` / `.red`, drawn as the row tint (`Common/RowTint.swift`).\n- The default row, `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/LegacyTopicRowView.swift:29-54`, has no flag icon; its own comment (`:21`) says \"this row shows by weight or tint only\". VoiceOver does get the state (`.accessibilityValue(spokenState)`, `:52`), so the gap is for sighted users.\n- `accessibilityDifferentiateWithoutColor` is read nowhere in `App/SwiftHFR`. The icon exists already for the experimental dense row (`Experimental/DenseRows/DenseRowMarkers.swift:40-48`, `FlagIconMark`).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nSame tint-only cue: `HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift:736` (`rowBackgroundTint(for:)`), drawn at `Common.swift:3677-3684`.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect**: accessibility, shared with legacy.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- When `@Environment(\\.accessibilityDifferentiateWithoutColor)` is on, show `FlagIconMark` before the title in the default row; the default look stays legacy's.\n- Mac check: Réglages iOS › Accessibilité › Différencier sans couleur on, a category list with the three flag types; also whether the light tint is visible at all on the card in light mode.\n\nRelated: #572 (state tints; this is the colour-only angle).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
